+## Window choice and the whole-year map (added 21 November 2026)
+
+The default fixed training window moved from January–April to May–August, which suits the European
+development data. In Paoay it is almost never clear: notebook 06's `four_month_windows.csv` shows
+1.2 % of active cropland with all eight May–August half-months clear in 2024 and 0 % in 2019–2023
+and 2025, against 100 % for January–April 2024. Notebooks 02–05 are therefore kept as the
+**January–April 2024 baseline** with their matching saved model; they were not rerun for May–August.
+
+[Transfer notebook 13](../notebooks/transfer/13_paoay_start_month_maps.ipynb) trains one fixed-window
+model per start month (development parcels only) and maps Paoay in each window's clearest year. The
+windows that score best in Europe (May–September) are 1–6 % clear in Paoay; the only fully clear one
+(January–April 2024) scores lowest in Europe and maps mostly potato. No window gives a crop mix close
+to the PSA Benguet shares.
+
+The proposed Paoay approach, pending team agreement, is the [improved pipeline](../notebooks/improved/README.md):
+whole-year harmonic Sentinel-2 features plus Sentinel-1 need no clear four-month window and classify
+every study pixel (notebook 04). It is still potato-biased and unvalidated. Its notebook 05 is a
+**statistical sampling design** for the January visit (stratified random by map class inside cropland,
+reserves, reference-area points), unlike the checklist below. Take its `visit_points.kml` and
+`field_sheet.csv` to the field; both omit predictions. Do not take the plan's `visit_plan.png`, which shows the map.
